Perfetto: check the successful OpenBSD getexecpath return value.

OpenBSD getexecpath(3) returns 0 on success and -1 on error. Preserve the
existing separate NetBSD sysctl path. OpenBSD runtime execution remains
unverified; this fix is based on the documented API contract.

Origin: EmberBSD (AI-assisted), not submitted upstream.

--- a/third_party/perfetto/src/base/utils.cc
+++ b/third_party/perfetto/src/base/utils.cc
@@ -263,7 +263,7 @@
 #if (OpenBSD >= 202610)
   char execpath[PATH_MAX];
   int ret = getexecpath(execpath, sizeof(execpath));
-  PERFETTO_CHECK(ret != 0);
+  PERFETTO_CHECK(ret == 0);
   self_path = std::string(execpath);
 #else
   char *buf;
